  "notes": [
    "This test data demonstrates a typical workflow execution flow",
    "First message is ExecutionSnapshotMessage with type='initial_snapshot' (sent when replay=0)",
    "Last message is ExecutionSnapshotMessage with type='final_snapshot' (sent when execution completes)",
    "Server disconnects WebSocket after sending final_snapshot",
    "ExecutionSnapshotMessage.execution uses the same Execution schema as REST API GET /executions/{id}?include=activities",
    "This enables unified UI processing logic for both WebSocket and REST data sources",
    "All messages include a timestamp field indicating when the event occurred",
    "Subsequent updates use ActivityPatchMessage with JSON Patch operations and timestamp",
    "Status updates use op=replace operations on /activities/{activity_id}/status",
    "Progress and iteration fields are added/updated/removed as needed",
    "Error details are added when activities fail using op=add",
    "event_id format is Valkey auto-generated stream ID: {milliseconds}-{sequence}",
    "Clients can replay from any event_id using replay parameter (e.g., ?replay=1691431234100-0)",
    "Edge status is derived client-side from source/target node status (no server broadcast for edges)"
  ]
